#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""fleet-health — verify signing, TCC, session and mesh health across the fleet.

Usage:
  tools/fleet-health [--host all|local|<id>]
                     [--check sign|no-adhoc|identifiers|tcc|authenticode|session|mesh|instances|bridge|loginbridge|all]
                     [--json] [--env PATH] [--watch N]

Reads scripts/fleet.env (same format as fleet-doctor / fleet-deploy.sh):
  FLEET_HOSTS="hackintosh macbookpro tiny11"
  FLEET_SSH_<id>=<ssh target|local>
  FLEET_SSH_USER_<id>=<user>          (optional)
  FLEET_OS_<id>=macos|windows         (optional; default: tiny11/win*/tiny* => windows)
  FLEET_ADDR_<id>=<host/ip>           (optional; address peers use for the mesh check)
  FLEET_MESH_PORT=24851               (optional; coordination-mesh port, NOT the
                                       KVM/Synergy port -- see the mesh check below)
  FLEET_DESKFLOW_PATH_macos=~/Desktop/deskflow   (where scripts/deskflow-ctl lives)
  FLEET_DESKFLOW_PATH_windows=C:/Users/alexh/Desktop/deskflow
  DESKFLOW_SIGN_THUMBPRINT=<sha1>     (Windows Authenticode thumbprint)

Checks:
  sign/no-adhoc/identifiers  codesign state of every Mach-O in the app bundles
                             plus /usr/local/bin/deskflow-prio (macOS)
  tcc                        TCC grants are cert-based and granted (macOS)
  authenticode               Authenticode thumbprint on every exe/dll (Windows)
  session                    deskflow-core loaded via launchd; Deskflow GUI and
                             Mouser processes running (Mouser is intentionally
                             not launchd-managed, so this is a process check)
  mesh                       every seat reaches every other seat on the
                             coordination-mesh port (always listening
                             regardless of role). NOT the KVM/Synergy port:
                             in auto-elect mode only the currently-elected
                             server binds that one, so checking it there
                             would fail on every client seat by design.
  instances                  `scripts/deskflow-ctl assert-single` on each host:
                             exactly one Deskflow core (owned by launchd / the
                             service) and one GUI from the canonical path, nothing
                             else. Exit 0 from the ctl = PASS.
  bridge                     the local Mouser bridge on 127.0.0.1:19795 answers
                             {"t":"status"} with attached:true and
                             peer:"deskflow-core" (macOS: nc -w2; Windows: the
                             ps1 collector via .NET TcpClient). Catches a core
                             that is running but silently in legacy/off mode.
  keys                       stuck-key sweeps in the core's own rotated log
                             (macOS; `[log] file=` from ~/Library/Deskflow/
                             Deskflow.conf, default ~/Library/Deskflow/
                             deskflow-core.log, plus its .1/.2 generations --
                             NOT ~/Library/Logs, which launchd routes to
                             /dev/null). Lines are ordered by their own
                             timestamp across generations; unstamped lines
                             are ignored and counted. FAIL on any "[keys]
                             stuck-release" (WARNING) line in the last 24 h --
                             the post-switch verifier had to release a
                             modifier nobody typed after a crossing. WARN on
                             "[keys] post-switch held=" (INFO) lines with no
                             release behind them, or when `[log] level` is
                             too quiet for those lines to ever land in the
                             file. SKIP when the log directory does not exist.
  loginbridge                the LoginWindow bridge agent (macOS): the plist
                             exists and lints, its program is the installed
                             bundle's deskflow-vhid-bridge and it passes
                             --calibrate, the log is mode 600 and holds no
                             keystrokes, and -- when passwordless sudo is
                             available -- launchctl reports the agent in the
                             loginwindow domain and the log shows the newest
                             bridge start reaching "virtual HID ready" within
                             30 s with no vhid connect_failed after it (else
                             the privileged parts are SKIP with the reason).

Environment overrides:
  DESKFLOW_EXPECT_AUTHORITY  expected `Authority=` prefix (default "Apple Development")
  DESKFLOW_EXPECT_TEAM       expected `TeamIdentifier=` (default: value on the main binary)

--watch N re-runs the selected checks every N seconds and prints only
transitions (PASS->FAIL / FAIL->PASS per host+check), each also raised as a
macOS notification (osascript). A new status must hold for two consecutive
passes before it counts, so one dropped ssh session does not flap. The first
pass prints the full table as the baseline. Ctrl-C exits 0.

Exit status is 0 only when every check on every host passes. stdlib only.
"""

